<p>President Trump renewed criticism of Pope Leo XIV ahead of Secretary of State Marco Rubio&#x27;s scheduled meeting with the pontiff at the Vatican on Thursday. In an interview with conservative commentator Hugh Hewitt, Trump accused Leo of helping Iran and &quot;endangering&quot; Catholics by, in Trump&#x27;s account, accepting an Iranian nuclear weapon. Several accounts said Pope Leo has not said Iran should have nuclear weapons; the pontiff has criticized the U.S.-Israeli war against Iran, called for peace and said the Catholic Church has long opposed all nuclear weapons. Rubio, a Catholic, said Tuesday that the visit was routine engagement with the Holy See and was not designed to ease tensions, citing issues such as humanitarian aid in Cuba and challenges facing Christians in Africa. The State Department said Rubio would meet Pope Leo and Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni during a two-day Italy visit. U.S. ambassador to the Holy See Brian Burch said he did not accept the idea that there was a &quot;deep rift&quot; between Washington and the Vatican.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/uNP2GSzIne7SOETAmQWDRfdLN9tyvxM0yrX4Gy3R7jygqQXgYZ-zUVofOIquLv2K39UKsN2dfaBMuqfin2E2iTVL10uuqeUqgJu2gUjyj6ObWdJMOeLoF8sys8x6KtQPTgDwUAuxJsT8Q7NSsbFwVUfBViA0pr8QwFIJyZi456Qne4iu5I4fS0cMgKSVG0HH1lAkbVfJrtUw0ccNgm_QYQLP-Jq5yhIE74W-b-CGUT7Uul4g2EYUDVDMw1MR6fqunqSOK8eXc0rTvemwMA' alt='Pope Leo XIV talks to journalists as he leaves his residence in Castel Gandolfo, on the outskirts of Rome, to return to the Vatican on Tuesday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Earlier criticism: In April, Trump called Pope Leo &quot;WEAK on Crime, and terrible for Foreign Policy&quot; and urged him to &quot;stop catering to the Radical Left&quot; in a Truth Social post.</li><li>Papal response: Leo said it was &quot;not in interest at all&quot; to debate Trump on the Middle East conflict and said he would continue to speak out against war.</li><li>Venue detail: Rubio is set to meet Pope Leo at the Vatican’s Apostolic Palace on Thursday morning.</li><li>Interview context: Hewitt raised Jimmy Lai, a Catholic pro-democracy leader in Hong Kong sentenced by China to 20 years, before Trump shifted back to complaints about the pope.</li></ul><blockquote>The mission of the Church is to preach the Gospel, to preach peace - Pope Leo XIV</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: Trump also criticized Leo’s comments about treating immigrants with respect, saying the pontiff’s words were making the world “less safe.” (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3352541/trump-renews-attacks-pope-leo-just-days-rubios-vatican-trip'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Pope Leo XIV: Leo said his remarks were grounded in Scripture and Church teaching rather than in a partisan argument with Trump. (<a href='https://444.hu/2026/05/06/trump-megint-hazudozott-a-paparol-akihez-most-kuldi-el-a-kulugyminiszteret'>444.hu</a>)</li><li>Secretary of State Marco Rubio: Rubio said he expected a “frank” meeting with Leo, while U.S. officials described the visit as a chance for direct dialogue. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/rubio-expects-frank-meeting-with-pope-as-trump-takes-fresh-potshots-at-leo/article70944405.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Italy&#x27;s foreign ministry: Foreign Minister Antonio Tajani said the pope&#x27;s words and actions promoted dialogue, human life and freedom, and said Italy&#x27;s government sought to advance similar values through diplomacy. (<a href='https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20260505-after-more-trump-criticisms-of-pontiff-italys-foreign-minister-says-attacks-on-pope-leo-not-acceptable/'>Middle East Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/inthenews/comments/1t4s8z7/trump_ripped_after_new_screed_against_pope_leo/'>Trump ripped after new screed against Pope Leo: ‘Endangering a lot of Catholics’</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde